{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.QCasimirClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.QCasimirClassicalLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Order.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.lean#L122-L135","doc":"**Classical limit of the Casimir eigenvalue**: as `q → 1`,\n`[j]_q · [j+1]_q → j · (j+1)`.  Combines two instances of\n`qNumberSym_classical_limit` with `Filter.Tendsto.mul`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-casimir-classical-limit","label":"prop:q-casimir-classical-limit","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.lean#L96-L120","doc":"**Theorem (L'Hôpital / polynomial continuity):\nsymmetric q-number classical limit `[n]_q → n` as `q → 1`.**\nFor `n ≥ 0`, `[n]_q = q^{-(n-1)} (q^{2n} - 1)/(q² - 1) = q^{-(n-1)} ∑ q^{2k}`.\nFor `n < 0`, similar logic applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym_classical_limit_nat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym_classical_limit_nat","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.lean#L63-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.lean#L51-L54","doc":"q-Casimir eigenvalue over `ℝ` — the `K := ℝ` specialisation of the\ngeneric `QCasimirEigenvalue` of `def:q-casimir`: `[j]_q · [j+1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-classical-limit.lean#L44-L49","doc":"Symmetric q-number over `ℝ` — the `K := ℝ` specialisation of the\ngeneric `qNumberSym` of `def:q-casimir`:\n`[n]_q = (qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ)/(q - q⁻¹)`. Re-stated locally so this block\ntypechecks standalone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}